      "body": "## Motivation\n\nIn `DeepseekMLAForwardMixin.forward_absorb_core`, the BF16 value projection writes into a transposed, non-contiguous view through `torch.bmm(..., out=...)`. TorchDynamo does not support `out=` with a non-contiguous output, so tracing `forward_absorb_core` with `torch.compile` or `torch.export` fails on this call.\n\nThis branch used to switch to the out-of-place form under the torch.compile piecewise CUDA graph runner (`is_in_tc_piecewise_cuda_graph()`). That check went away with the runner, which leaves every other compile path on the `out=` form.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdd an `elif torch.compiler.is_compiling():` branch ahead of the eager fallback that computes the same product out-of-place:\n\n```python\nattn_bmm_output = torch.bmm(attn_output.transpose(0, 1), self.w_vc)\nattn_bmm_output = attn_bmm_output.transpose(0, 1).flatten(1, 2)\n```\n\n`torch.compiler.is_compiling()` is `False` outside tracing, so eager mode and CUDA graph capture keep the existing `out=` path.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nSame values as the eager branch. With full-graph `torch.compile` decode on an out-of-tree platform: DeepSeek-R1-0528 (TP8) GSM8K (5-shot, flexible-extract) 0.9621 (reference 0.9651 +/- 0.0107); GLM-5.2-FP8 (TP8) in graph mode and DeepSeek-R1-0528 (TP8) in eager mode also pass.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Formatting: black-stable (ruff-format compatible).\n- [ ] Unit tests: none added; happy to add one if wanted.\n",
